d by the muscles that it  targets what kind of workout it fits  into or that's Push Pull legs or even  cardio importantly though I also  categorize all the exercises based on  where I need to be to train them so  although I can use the exercise at home  whether it needs specific equipment I  can only get it game but that's  something I can do outdoors with just  the kind of environment so that I can  use filters in order to show all the  exercises that I can do in a given  location that's going to Target the  things I want to Target and get the  results I want to get then I can select  my favorite ones and I can easily look  and see which muscles are being targeted  what the traits being worked are and I  can swap different ones out or choose  which ones I want to do that day this is  the system I'll be linking to in the  description you can check that out for  yourself if you're interested keep in  mind though that this is designed to be  flexible and it's also written for me  not for you guys there's no sets and  Reps a lot of them are going to sound  odd or weirdly specific if you want a  structured routine with sets and Reps  and things that's based along the same  principles then of course check out the  protein performance system which I'll  put a link to in the description down  below there's a sale on right now for  January so yeah good time to check it  out if you're interested  in terms of the channel going forwards  and the brand there's a few things that  I am looking to do a bit differently the  first is kind of like the behind the  scenes stuff in terms of management I  want to take a slightly more hands-off  approach and don't worry I don't mean  I'm not going to be presenting I don't  mean I'm not going to be editing and  doing all those things I want to do a  little bit less emailing I don't really  enjoy that side of things I like to just  get down and write and I really want to  put more emphasis on the blog itself and  write more blog posts because I am a  heart a writer I love deep dives into  subjects that wouldn't necessarily  perform well on YouTube so I want to do  more of that and if I'm also going to be  placing more emphasis on my training and  doing that at the start of my days then  I'm gonna have less time of course to be  doing admin and stuff which like I say  I'm not good at and don't want to do  anyways there's so many emails so many  opportunities they're just sitting in my  inbox and people are getting frustrated  with me because I just don't have time  to film all this stuff so I'm hopefully  going to be working with an admin  assistant someone who can do some of  that stuff with me I'm going to be  looking into ways to streamline this  process and even like Outsourcing things  like I'm doing shorts and I'm hoping to  Outsource the editing things like that  just there's a little bit less on my  plate there I can focus more on the  things that I hope bring real value and  I actually enjoy doing and be a little  bit less stressed and exhausted and like  I say the channel has been taking a  little bit of a dive in terms of  viewership and view count so I need to  experiment with different types of  content on the site and see what's going  to be more successful it's really hard  balancing act because you don't want to  sell out obviously and just do all the  stuff that you think YouTube wants you  to do but at the same time you do need  the views and especially because you  know it's my income and it's how I  support my family and if I want to do  things like Outsourcing some of those  things then I need more income in order  to be able to support that so yeah one  of the big lessons for me then is really  managing my recovery and as I've always  talked about on this channel not just  thinking about your exercise and your  training in isolation you have to think  about the bigger picture and your health  overall if you're not sleeping then you  need to train less and if you have a  very physically demanding job then you  need to train less or you need to find  ways to fit that training in around that  demanding job and if that demanding job  is already taken care of some aspects of  your strength and performance then your  goal is to bring up the rest of your  physique and the rest of your  performance to match if you think about  your training and your lifestyle not as  separate things but as part of one  bigger picture then you can get far  better results in the end and that's why  it's a really useful strategy to not  just think about specific goals I'm  going to do this and I'm gonna eat this  and I'm gonna you know exercise like  this think in terms of how you're going  to redesign your entire routine and your  entire lifestyle to facilitate the goals  that you want and for me that often  means implementing rules think about all  the different aspects that might be  filtering in on that whether it's your  mental health whether it's your diet  whether it's your sleep and Recovery  whether it's your career whatever it is  it does have some impact on every other  aspect of your life  anyways guys I hope you found this  useful and interesting in some way if  nothing else it shows you a kind of road  map what I'm hoping to achieve then you  guys can follow along with me and watch  my training and see if I'm actually  achieving and following through on those  goals hopefully it gives me a little bit  of accountability I'd love to know your  goals and Ambitions for 2023 breathing  training in business that kind of stuff  let me know in the comments down below  either way thank you so much for  watching this one guys and I'll see you  next time  bye for now
 

